thread:
Priya (AM): NewBridge wants a POC to replace CompetitorX's generate endpoint. Big asks: identical stop-token handling, streaming chunk parity, token accounting that matches their billing, SSO (SAML) + BYOK later. They also want a tiny adapter so their callers don't change.
Sam (Solutions): List of POC gates: 1) Response envelope compatibility (including streaming frames), 2) stop-token & partial chunk behavior parity, 3) token accounting match on canonical prompts, 4) security signoffs (DPA + export controls), 5) latency within 1.5x competitor in our staging region.
Rohit (Presales): I'll curate 14 prompts: 6 summarization, 4 extraction, 2 code rewrite, 2 long-context edge cases with stop tokens mid-stream. We'll include a fuzz set. We'll run side-by-side with streaming enabled so we can compare chunk boundaries.
Dana (ML Eng): Important note: CompetitorX's streaming protocol emits an initial meta frame, then partial "delta" text frames and a final "done" with usage. Their tokenizer treats certain Unicode ligatures as single tokens which changes billing. Expect token delta ~3-9% depending on inputs. We'll add a tokenizer-normalize pass to reduce that variance.
Kim (Security): Questions: Do they require customer-managed CA for TLS in staging? Do they need VPC peering / private link? Legal asked for DPA + export control review before we ship raw prompts.
Priya (AM): NewBridge: staging OK with platform-managed KMS; production must be BYOK + HSM option. They will request SAML metadata and IP allowlist. They also asked if we can mirror CompetitorX's streaming envelope so their SDKs don't break.
Sam (Solutions): We can provide a lightweight shim that mirrors streaming frames. Example (pseudo):
```
// CompetitorX streaming frames
{ "type":"meta", "id":"r1" }
{ "type":"delta", "text":"Hello" }
{ "type":"delta", "text":" world" }
{ "type":"done", "usage": {"tokens":42} }
// Redwood streaming shim frames
{ "frame_type":"meta","request_id":"r1" }
{ "frame_type":"chunk","content":"Hello" }
{ "frame_type":"chunk","content":" world" }
{ "frame_type":"end","usage":{"total_tokens":42} }
```
This keeps their client code intact.
Rohit (Presales): Acceptance criteria draft: mean token delta <= 9% on canonical set, streaming chunk sequence identical for first 80% of generations, semantic parity (human spot check >= 92%), staging latency <= 1.5x competitor, security signoff completed.
Dana (ML Eng): For parity tuning we'll expose a "compat_stream" variant that adjusts tokenizer normalization + repetition_penalty and enforces the same stop-token semantics (including how we truncate partial chunks). We'll commit seed + exact runtime flags in the test repo.
Kim (Security): Blockers: Legal needs a DPA signed and export-control triage for prompts that mention hardware designs. Also confirm whether NewBridge needs SOC2 + ISO docs attached. I'll prepare the security Q packet and checklist for BYOK onboarding.
infra-bot: staging cluster provisioned: newbridge-poc-staging | egress IPs: 18.44.55.99, 18.44.55.100
Priya (AM): NewBridge also asked about pricing: can we offer a 45-day trial credit and a graduated commit for Dedicated? They want an example calc showing token-delta impact.
Sam (Solutions): Yes. We'll show hosted vs dedicated: include a small calculator in the deck (example: if token delta +6% on 20M tokens/month -> +1.2M tokens cost at hosted rates; dedicated per-token is lower). I'll draft the pricing ramp: 45-day trial credits, months 2-3 30% discount on committed usage, month4+ standard committed pricing.
Rohit (Presales): I'll prepare the Postman collection + a stream-acceptance runner that connects to CompetitorX and our shim, captures frames, and outputs a TSV with: prompt, competitor_tokens, redwood_tokens, token_delta_pct, num_frames_match, latency_ms.
Dana (ML Eng): Will include model variants: quantized-default, fp16, compat_stream. Also include a forced-pretokenize pass for emoji/ligature normalization. I'll record commit hash + seed.
Kim (Security): Action: I'll draft security answers (KMS steps, audit log format, retention policy <=30d), confirm BYOK HSM steps, and ask Legal to start DPA.
Priya (AM): Scheduling kickoff Thurs 9:30am PT. Action owners: @Rohit test harness, @Sam pricing + shim spec, @Dana variants + seed, @Kim security + legal loop. Keep updates here; ping me if we hit regressions.
Sam (Solutions): Noted. If streaming-chunk diffs exceed tolerance we'll open a tuning sprint and consider a small client-side polyfill for stop-token edgecases.
Priya (AM): Thanks everyone — keeping thread as async source of truth.
